From: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] xfrm: release policy device reference after ops withdrawal

A policy may remain referenced after xfrm_dev_policy_flush() unlinks it.
If a device withdraws its XFRM operations before the final policy put,
xfrm_dev_policy_free() skips both the optional driver callback and the
netdev_put(). The latter leaks the policy's device reference and can keep
device unregistration waiting indefinitely.

Keep the driver callback conditional on available operations, but always
clear the policy's device pointer and release its reference on destruction.
This keeps the final-reference lifetime and callback-before-put ordering.

Fixes: 919e43fad516 ("xfrm: add an interface to offload policy")
Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
--- a/include/net/xfrm.h
+++ b/include/net/xfrm.h
@@ -2195,8 +2195,8 @@
 	struct xfrm_dev_offload *xdo = &x->xdo;
 	struct net_device *dev = xdo->dev;
 
-	if (dev && dev->xfrmdev_ops) {
-		if (dev->xfrmdev_ops->xdo_dev_policy_free)
+	if (dev) {
+		if (dev->xfrmdev_ops && dev->xfrmdev_ops->xdo_dev_policy_free)
 			dev->xfrmdev_ops->xdo_dev_policy_free(x);
 		xdo->dev = NULL;
 		netdev_put(dev, &xdo->dev_tracker);
